      "text": "ObsAwareData methods > 3. Reliability flag rules > 3.3 NSSP emergency department visits\n- **Trend label coverage.** `ed_trend_category` is `observed_low_coverage` when CDC's label is `Data Unavailable` or `Limited Data`. Other labels are `observed_valid`.\n- **Anomaly.** `ed_visit_percent_smoothed` is flagged `flagged_anomalous` with the same relative-change rule as NHSN, applied within each region and pathogen, using the state's NSSP threshold. The raw (unsmoothed) percent is not anomaly-flagged.\n- **Participation.** NSSP publishes no visit-count denominator, so coverage is approximated with CDC's county facility-participation map of 2026-08-06.\n  - An HSA is `reduced_participation` (flag `observed_low_coverage`) if at least one member county does not have \"recent data in NSSP\": either a mix of contributing and non-contributing counties, or no contributing county at all.\n  - It is `full_participation` otherwise."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "oad_methods#4",
      "doc_id": "oad_methods",
      "text": "ObsAwareData methods > 2. Geography\n- **State:** identified by its two-digit FIPS code.\n- **Health service area (HSA):** the sub-state unit in which CDC publishes NSSP data. It is a multi-county region, and every member county shares one value, so HSA values are not independent county measurements. Some HSAs appear in the source with no ED values at any time.\n- **Wastewater site:** the unit in which CDC publishes wastewater data. A site can serve several counties, and a few serve counties in two states; a site is listed under the state given by the source. Sites are not split, weighted, or reassigned to counties or HSAs in these tables.\n- **Census:** state level only. No official correspondence exists between HSAs or wastewater service areas and Census geographies, so no population weighting to those units is attempted."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "oad_data_sources#5",
      "doc_id": "oad_data_sources",
      "text": "ObsAwareData data sources > 2. Emergency department visits: NSSP\n- **Geography:** State, and CDC health service areas (HSAs) within the state. HSAs are identified by their NCI HSA code. An HSA is a multi-county region; every member county carries the same value. The national row is excluded.\n- **Supplementary coverage file:** CDC's NSSP county facility-participation map ([coverage-map.csv](https://www.cdc.gov/nssp/documents/coverage-map.csv)), downloaded on 2026-08-06. It is used only to derive the ED `participation_status` field (see [METHODS.md](METHODS.md)). It is a single point-in-time snapshot, not a weekly history."
